",\"text\":\"Both work; choice depends on context. Subtitles are faster and cheaper for social media and corporate intranets. Voiceover suits broadcast, longer-form content, and audiences with lower literacy or accessibility needs. Many brands use hybrid: Swiss German or English voiceover with French/Italian subtitles for efficiency.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What's the best way to hire voiceover talent for Swiss German, French, and Italian?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Work with a Swiss post-production agency or casting director familiar with regional dialects and corporate tone. Avoid hiring non-Swiss French or German speakers—regional authenticity matters. Record all voiceover tracks in a single studio session to maintain acoustic consistency across languages.\"}}]}]}"}></script>
